@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>This is an educational project for Mobile Application Development course.</p>

<h3>Data Collection</h3>
<p>This application collects the following user information:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Username and password (stored in plain text for educational purposes only)</li>
    <li>Game completion times</li>
    <li>Premium user status</li>
</ul>

<h3>Data Usage</h3>
<p>User data is used solely for:</p>
<ul>
    <li>User authentication</li>
    <li>Leaderboard rankings</li>
    <li>Application functionality demonstration</li>
</ul>

<h3>Security Notice</h3>
<div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">
    <strong>⚠️ Educational Project Only</strong><br>
    This application is designed for learning purposes and should not be used in production environments. 
    Passwords are stored in plain text without encryption. In production applications, always use proper 
    authentication mechanisms such as ASP.NET Core Identity with password hashing.
</div>

<h3>Data Retention</h3>
<p>User data is stored in a MySQL database and retained for the duration of the course assignment.</p>

<h3>Contact</h3>
<p>For questions about this privacy policy, please contact the development team (Group 7).</p>

<p class="text-muted mt-4"><small>Last updated: December 31, 2025</small></p>